enerators closed (queue 339)"] [227 1 "// OpImpl implements an operation outside step's switch (PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): it pops and pushes f's"] [228 1 "// stack itself and returns (nil, nil) to go on; (nil, err) raises; (nil, *pushFrame) runs a Python"] [229 1 "// function's frame next; (v, nil) makes f return v (a generator's yield sets f.Suspended first)."] [232 1 "// opImpls are the operations registered by the files that own them (§9), each by its file's init:"] [233 1 "// RegisterOp(OpLoadAttr, ...). An operation of step's switch is never looked up here."] [236 1 "// RegisterOp sets op's implementation; a second one is a programming error (one owner per operation)."] [244 1 "// pushFrame is step's signal that the instruction called a Python function: not an exception."] [247 1 "// callStack is call [N KWNAMES]: the callable under its N arguments on f's stack (the last len(kwnames) of them"] [248 1 "// keywords), all popped; a Python function's frame (a bound method's, its self first) made from the arguments"] [249 1 "// where they are on the stack and returned as the thread's *pushFrame, a generator made, or any other callable"] [250 1 "// called and its value pushed (202b: the arguments were copied off the stack, then again with self in front)."] [254 22 "// sys.monitoring's CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [266 24 "// the callable's slot holds self: the arguments are self's and the stack's"] [279 4 "// a built-in method bound to its object (BuiltinType's call slot): its arguments made at once with self"] [280 4 "// first (queue 210: they were copied off the stack, then again behind self)"] [296 51 "// next(gen()): the generator dies at the return (queue 297)"] [319 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [328 1 "// directMax bounds the direct calls (callDirect) nested on the thread's Go stack at once: each holds its caller's Go"] [329 1 "// frames while its callee runs, so a deeper chain (a recursion past it, up to any recursion limit) goes on as pushed"] [330 1 "// frames, in the innermost loop, with no Go frames per Python call (queue 216d)."] [333 1 "// enter is a call's callee frame (made, its arguments bound) run from f: when f and the callee are both compiled,"] [334 1 "// directly by f's own Go code (callDirect: its value pushed on f's stack, or its exception returned); else returned"] [335 1 "// as the thread's *pushFrame, read by runFrames before the thread's next call."] [344 1 "// callDirect runs callee, a compiled function's frame called by f's compiled code (queue 216d, the user's (a) on"] [345 1 "// 216's DECISION 1): a loop of its own (runFrames, direct) with callee its entry frame, entered as runFrames enters a"] [346 1 "// pushed frame (f_back f, the recursion limit's check raising in f, the eval breaker's error in callee, no C level),"] [347 1 "// so its exception unwinds through callee's handlers and leaves it with callee's traceback entry, then f's code"] [348 1 "// returns it and f's loop adds f's; its value pushed on f's stack, or callInit's instance (an __init__ returning"] [349 1 "// anything but None the TypeError raised in f), as runFrames pushes a returning pushed frame's."] [359 1 "// runDirect is callDirect's run of callee from the running frame's compiled code: its value (callInit's instance for"] [360 1 "// an __init__), or its exception, returned to that code."] [379 1 "// callInit is the call of a class whose __init__ runs in the caller's loop (initInline; queue 210, CPython 3.14's"] [380 1 "// CALL_ALLOC_AND_ENTER_INIT): the instance made by the type's __new__ (object's) from the arguments where they are"] [381 1 "// on f's stack (k the first's position), then __init__'s frame with the instance as self in the class's slot,"] [382 1 "// returned as the thread's *pushFrame; runFrames pushes the instance when that frame returns None (TypeType's call"] [383 1 "// slot's check otherwise, raised at the call)."] [401 1 "// initInline i